# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
# .env holds the ntfy topic, which is a bearer secret: anyone who knows it can
# read every push. .env.example is the committed template and is the one
# exception.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Virtualenvs -----------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Caches and build artifacts --------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# --- OS ---------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store

# --- Logs -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run logs are ephemeral; the committed source of truth is data/postings.jsonl
# and data/run-report.json. Keep the directory, drop the contents.
#
# These also carry a partially-redacted ntfy topic and, on a scoring or Sheets
# failure, an exception message that can contain a request URL. They must never
# be committed.
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep
*.log

# --- Databases --------------------------------------------------------------
# No SQLite file is ever committed. The database is a rebuildable cache:
# data/postings.jsonl and data/baseline.txt are the committed source of truth,
# because SQLite rewrites a multi-MB blob on every commit even for a one-row
# change, in a repo that commits every half hour.
#
# The sidecar files matter as much as the database itself - they cause merge
# conflicts and can corrupt the committed .db when replayed out of order.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Conditional-request validators (ETag / Last-Modified) live in
# data/http-cache.db, covered by the rule above. Rebuildable at the cost of one
# full fetch, so never committed - the poll workflow carries the file between
# runs with actions/cache instead, which is the only reason a CI run ever sends
# a conditional GET.

# --- Personal data ----------------------------------------------------------
# Personal eligibility facts (work authorization, clearance, grad year).
# profile/local.example.yml is the committed template.
profile/local.yml

# Local application-tracking scratch, exported from the Sheets backlog.
data/backlog-review.csv

# --- Working notes, not part of the public repo -----------------------------
# Build history, handoff notes and the generated weekly rollup. They carry
# personal detail and stale figures that contradict the README, and none of
# them is needed to run or understand the pipeline. Kept on disk, out of git.
# EVAL.md is regenerated by `make eval`; the other two are hand-written.
FEEDBACK.md
HANDOFF.md
EVAL.md

# The filled-in candidate profile. profile/resume.example.md is the committed
# template; the real one carries a name, school and graduation date.
profile/resume.md
